.TH CENTCOM 1 "" "centcom 0.1.0 (contract 1.2.0)" "Centcom"
.SH NAME
centcom \- the terminal app and print mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B centcom [options] | centcom \-p "task"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the terminal app in the current folder, or with \-p runs one task and prints the answer. Centcom drives your own Claude Code or Codex; it never sees your login.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-print [task]
run once, print the answer and exit (no screen); piped input is added to the prompt
.TP
.B \-\-output\-format <text|json|stream\-json>
what \-p prints (default text)
.TP
.B \-\-engine <claude\-code|codex|demo>
choose the agent engine (default: claude\-code if installed)
.TP
.B \-\-demo
scripted demo agent (no login, no model)
.TP
.B \-\-demo\-team
with \-\-demo: also show two pretend teammates
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-continue
continue the most recent conversation in this folder
.TP
.B \-\-resume <id>
continue a specific saved conversation
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save
do not save this conversation or your prompt history
.TP
.B \-\-no\-checkpoints
do not snapshot the folder before each prompt
.TP
.B \-\-model <name>
model to use (same ids as /model)
.TP
.B \-\-mode <default|plan|acceptEdits|bypassPermissions>
start in a permission mode
.TP
.B \-\-dangerously\-skip\-permissions
never ask: run commands and edit files freely (alias: \-\-yolo)
.TP
.B \-\-mascot <large|small|off>
Cento size (default: auto from terminal height)
.TP
.B \-\-cento\-color <violet|red|yellow|green|brown>
Cento's color
.TP
.B \-\-theme <dark|light>
Graphite (default) or Paper (for light terminals)
.TP
.B \-\-colors <truecolor|256|16|never>
force a colour tier (NO_COLOR is honoured)
.TP
.B \-\-debug
write detailed logs to ~/.centcom/logs/centcom.log
.TP
.B \-\-no\-motion
turn animation off (also CENTCOM_REDUCED_MOTION=1; the older CENTCOM_REDUCE_MOTION works too)
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
print the version
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
print this help
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
centcom
.fi
.PP
.nf
cat error.log | centcom \-p "what went wrong?"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
centcom help, https://centcom.dev/docs
